              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "LILKITTEN79"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I make almost the same recipe for all our cook outs and holidays. The only thing different is I also add to mine pepperoni, cauliflower, chopped up cucumber, and use shells instead of spaghetti.The shells hold the dressing better."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Butterfly Flutterby"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Off and on I have kept this in my fridge for my children to snack on for years. I use parmesan instead of cheddar and vary the veggies. Often I will toss in quartered pepperoni slices or ham cubes. Thank you.",
            "datePublished": "2005-12-11T07:51:24.640Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "DREGINEK"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Good summer noodle salad. I went and bought a pepperoni and hard salami stick (the smallest ones I could find) and cut them into cubes and added it. Also, I LOVE Italian dressing but find that a TBLS of white sugar keeps the heartburn away.",
            "datePublished": "2008-06-19T13:10:20.143Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Lisa Taylor"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Wow...I loved this recipe. The only changes I made was to use penne pasta instead of spaghetti, and feta cheese instead of cheddar. I will definitely make this again!",
            "datePublished": "2008-06-19T13:00:19.960Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Heather Calhoun"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this to take to my aunt's house for dinner on Friday evening. I made double the recipe and this dish was gone in 30 minutes. I did modify the recipe a little. I added a little distilled vinegar and a little more italian dressing. I also added celery salt, sugar, seasoning salt, onion powder, dried basil, and used finely shredded parmesan cheese instead of cheddar cheese. I also broke the noodles in thirds so it would be easier to stir up and used tongs to serve it. It took me quite a while to mix all the ingredients together because I was making so much. I just wanted to make sure everything was mixed up and every noodle had flavor in it. It sat for about 6 hours and it was so good and seasoned. I will definitely be making this again.",
            "datePublished": "2009-09-08T05:45:46.063Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Chelsea"
            },
            "reviewBody": "this is a very good pasta salad. i would use less bell pepper, and grate the onions so its less chunky. i also use parmesan instead of cheddar.",
            "datePublished": "2007-11-23T18:13:57.967Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Mary Ellen Curtin"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I use angel hair spaghetti and the salad supreme seasoning instead of the italian seasoning. I do break the spaghetti in half before cooking. I cube my cheese not shred as it doesn't get stuck together. I prefer provolone and do add some parmesan cheese. I also use cherry or grape tomatoes cut in half.",
            "datePublished": "2014-09-03T07:05:42.310Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Barb"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Oh man was this ever good! I used grape tomatoes and the Salad Supreme seasoning. I made it the night before but added the shredded cheddar cheese just before serving so it wouldn't get too soft or mushy. Definitely a keeper but the next time I make it, I might try a different pasta.",
            "datePublished": "2011-07-25T14:29:27.467Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "LYNNC51"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I have had a similar recipe for years. It's: 1 (1 lb 6 oz) pkg spaghetti\n1 small bottle Italian dressing\n1/2-2/3 of a jar of Johnny's Dock Salad Elegance\n1/4 cup wine vinegar\n1 green pepper, chopped fine\n1 cucumber, chopped\n2 tomatoes, chopped\nBoil and cook spaghetti. Mix all ingredients together and marinate for 24 hours in refrigerator.",
            "datePublished": "2008-06-22T17:57:19.610Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "scooter"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I had 1 Cup leftover spaghetti so I simply cut it up, popped it in microwave with a little added water to plump it up. Then added the ingredients adjusted for 1 Cup of spaghette and also added a sprinkle of onion power/garlic powder, some chopped fresh parsley, and used 2-3TBSP grated parmesan (instead of shredded cheddar). This is a keeper for any leftover pasta!",
            "datePublished": "2006-08-29T11:07:46.700Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Saveur"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was a nice addition to our 4th of July potluck. I used red and yellow tomato and added black olives and parmesean cheese per previous reviewers suggestion. Skipped the raw onion, just personal preference, but added a little onion powder for taste. Thanks for your nice submission.",
            "datePublished": "2009-07-05T05:08:41.913Z"
          },
